good morning Ross how are you morning  Dan doing great thanks can you sum up  sort of when you got that feeling that  this was going to be a different game  different Vikings team showing up last  night probably not until you know fools  hit the bomb to house on Jeffery and the  Eagle started you know when was 21-7  because before that was right after the  Derek Barnett strip sack of keenum  because up until that point I mean the  Vikings marched on that first drive I  thought the Eagles might be in trouble  and I still wonder what would have  happened and again I wish we could have  an alternate reality and see what  happened in that game if Chris Long  doesn't hit Keenan's arm and lead to the  pick six for Patrick Robinson but after  that it just seemed like it went all  downhill for the Vikings I've seen some  of the quotes from Terrence Newman a  former teammate of mine other guys Kenny  had no energy or no life and maybe  that's a carryover from what happened  the week before but I would have thought  Dan if that was a carryover that that  would be reflected in the start of the  game and it was it I mean the Vikings  marched right down the field yeah and  then it's all of a sudden you had to  pick six and then all of a sudden you  had the the touchdown I I thought the  Torrey Smith touchdown was the one that  was sort of like uh-oh you guys are you  guys are in for a long long night here  yeah I just can't believe what I saw you  know I live outside of Philadelphia grew  up here so I watched every snap at our  Eagles game and it's unbelievable banned  how bad Nick Foles was against the  Raiders and the Cowboys and then for him  to play that well I mean he really he  really did look like Carson Wentz last  night he made Carson Wentz type of plays  it's incredible man he's got to be up  there when you think about the 2013  season he had and they're like what do  you do with the Rams a couple years  later he's up there in terms of the  all-time check on high quarterback in  NFL history because he's got his eyes  are really high and his lows are really  low as a former NFL offensive lineman  tell me what you see with that defensive  front with the Eagles and what you think  how they play that when they  face New England well it's what's so  impressive about them and why I think an  early tip here is that the Patriots will  do a lot of no huddle is that it's their  depth it's that they just come in you  and wait I mean Chris Long doesn't even  start you know so if you are Bill  Belichick and Tom Brady and the Vikings  tried to do this a little bit at times  last night what makes them so special is  that they bring the guys in and waves  and I can remember even when I was in  New England II was in Buffalo and we had  a good defensive line with Katt Williams  Sam Adams  that used to be fellow second brady's  thing cut a tire out because they don't  have as much depth at D tackle so try to  tire out  Fletcher Cox and Timmy Jernigan and also  not let the Eagle sub when they have  every guy that comes in is that fresh  and that good it just kind of it just  kind of beats you down I don't know if  it's conscious or subconscious but a lot  of times when I was playing Dan he's  bringing it back up like a rotational  guy and you kind of be happy cuz right  okay this guy's not as good as a guy  we're just calling it for the Eagles  there's just there's just no let-up if I  take away Brady and foals and I compare  these two teams now I know you can't do  this on game day but let's just for  entertainment purposes who's got the  better team Philadelphia or New England  if I take away the quarterbacks oh the  Eagles the Eagles especially you know  with no element which by the way is  pretty incredible when the Eagles don't  have their Hall of Fame left tackle you  know their best running back probably in  Sproles their best linebacker I would  argue in Jordan Hicks their best special  teamer and Maragos I mean what what Rose  was done with this roster is incredible  I would say the Eagles I mean they're  better at almost every position probably  in that corner but definitely the Eagles  in my mind the Brady performance that he  said after the fact hey I don't want to  sound arrogant but you know I this  wasn't a big deal but it certainly felt  like a big deal leading up to this game  so how do you rank this Brady  performance yesterday afternoon  I've almost lost track at this point in  you know I kind of reformed just because  I was there and oh five and oh six and I  was his teammate and I mean every time  he does another amazing thing it makes  me a little bit cooler somehow I don't  know I mean eight Super Bowls in 16  years of playing 75% conference  championship games and clearly the  stitches weren't that much of an impact  in but didn't help me it does as a guy  that loves to practice he is the most  intense practice player I ever played  with so the fact that he wasn't able to  practice on Thursday that would drive  him bonkers I mean he would he would  absolutely be feeding about that he's  intense I mean he used to get intense  with me about snapping the ball to him I  mean he'd be like Ross has to be great  every time woody snap I mean you know I  was 26 pins and I've been playing  offensive line since sixth grade and  episode or every practice you snapped  the ball and it's like it's just what  you do it's kind of stupid it's like you  just do it because that's what you do at  practice you didn't want it to be a good  step or a great snap he wanted a perfect  I mean the guy is a total psycho in  every aspect of life and so even if the  stitches you know weren't that big of a  deal I mean it doesn't make it easier it  doesn't make it easier to throw a  football with ten stitches in your hand  or whatever he had would you rather lose  like the Vikings did or the Jags did Wow  I would say like the Vikings did because  because then you could be like man it  just wasn't our day and falls play out  of his mind  the Jags you can actually point to so  many play like in the Jags locker room  and on the plane those guys are all  thinking about that one or two plays  that if they had done something  different they could be playing in the  Super Bowl the Vikings are just drinking  beers being like holy crap that sucked  I'll leave you with this who has a  better chance to stay with their  respective teams Case Keenum or Blake  bortles  Blake bortles III I think well I think  both are both those guys will be with  their teams next year I don't know how  Jacksonville for Minnesota you can get  rid of either one of those guys but I  thought bortles was really impressive  yesterday you know Keenum had his worst  game in a while but portals back-to-back  games against Roethlisberger and Brady  on the road meaning I doesn't throw a  good ball ban but there's more to  playing the quarterback position than  just how pretty your ball is I mean his  playmaking ability and you know the way  he's able to move around I think he  makes up for it I think bortles  is going to be the jagged guy for the  next couple years Thank You Ross we'll  see in Minneapolis absolutely can't wait  there thanks for having me it's Ross  Tucker former lineman now working for  Westwood One also NBC Sports Network  working the NFC title game last night  for more Dan Patrick show to the  audience channel 239 on DirecTV or  download the Dan Patrick show app  [Music]

